  "findings": "Re-issued binding capture for the unchanged generic navigation block against the V2b candidate; the block's CSS, marker and rationale are untouched. The navigation state force-displays the submenus for geometry probing, so the frames show overlapping blank panels by design. Directly inspected the with/without frames at 320px index 2 and 390px index 3: without the block, the measured panel is clipped at the right viewport edge and the document overflows (width 359 at 320px, 452 at 390px; off-right 39.44px and 62.08px, identical to the original certification); with the candidate, every panel sits inside the viewport and all 16 measured rows show off-left 0 and off-right 0. The generic block's certified geometry is unchanged under the new candidate."
